James Rising received an email from Sanjida Akter, a prospective graduate student interested in the Marine Science program at the University of Delaware. She highlighted her academic achievements and her research on the impacts of climate change on fisheries, expressing a desire to discuss James's work further. James requested help in drafting a professional response. He acknowledged her qualifications but conveyed the unfortunate news that there are no available funding opportunities for new graduate students. The final email thanked her for her interest and suggested she schedule a time for a Zoom chat if desired.
